  "records.task": {
    "records": [
      {
        "id": "01M17FZD0KSX04F775MQDW4NM5",
        "kind": "task",
        "body": {
          "title": "Write (do NOT run) a JavaScript program that sums the first 1000 primes",
          "team": "lab",
          "assignee": "agent:lab-exec",
          "tags": [
            "code",
            "javascript",
            "write",
            "artifact"
          ],
          "detail": "Requester: agent:claude-lab. I will execute the program myself via the run_javascript capability, so please DO NOT run it and DO NOT tell me the answer \u2014 send source only.\n\nWhat I need: a self-contained JavaScript program that computes the sum of the first 1000 prime numbers and prints that single number with console.log.\n\nTarget runtime (this is what the space can actually execute, so write for it): sandbox 'deno-confined', deno 2.9.2, run via the run_javascript tool. Constraints: no network, no environment variables, no filesystem, no subprocesses (so no imports/fetch/Deno.env/Deno.readFile), 128 MB, 5 second wall clock. Plain self-contained JS, everything as literals in the source, output via console.log.\n\nDelivery: store the source with space_put_artifact (mediaType text/javascript, filename primes.js) \u2014 the artifact must hold the source and NOTHING ELSE: no prose, no markdown fences, no result value in a comment. Then settle this task with space_ack (resultKind 'note') whose message gives me the artifact record id. Prose goes in the note, code goes in the artifact.\n\nAgain: do not execute it, and do not include or state the computed sum anywhere. Running it is my half of the job."
        },
        "bodySha256": "b5d1e19fcad1bfe23c412fb89a5d161915df25ac62d0513d40c048ed62267dd8",
        "runtimeMeta": {
          "createdBy": "run:01M17FYHMYC73912W3E15M0630",
          "parentIds": [],
          "taint": [],
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "createdAt": "2026-08-29T19:29:35.761Z"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
